Prithee, let us speak of this matter with a mind so quick, that thou art well advised to learn the art of cooking, for threefold reasons shall I list them to thee:

First, by virtue of it, the body shall be nourished in sustenance, thus keeping thee warm against the biting winds of winter;
Secondly, 'tis a craft that makes thee to see the very visage of things as they are, so that thou mayst know the difference between the sweet and the sour, the savory and the piteous;
